rows.en:
"Commander, it has been a long time, sir. It is I, ·☆·☆★·, currently on a special mission under your secret orders, Commander."
"·☆·☆★☆☆·★·"
The Commander was speaking in some incomprehensible language.{p}

{f:I|I} thought to myself.
Looking like that, he was already so suspicious it was off the charts, so it was a little late to fuss over the language now, {f:wasn't it|wasn't it}...
No, I mustn't sweat the small stuff.{p}

A tremendous flash and a shock wave slammed into {f:me|me}.
The impact sent {f:me|me} flying backward.
{f:I|I} couldn't understand what had happened.{p}

Tomorrow I'm going to ask Hino.
Just what he meant by all this...
Honestly, give me a break.{p}

"You've found out my secret. Sorry, but I'm gonna have to mess with your memory."
With that, Shindo held his hand over {f:my|my} forehead.
{f:I|I} felt myself growing faint.{p}

{f:It's|It's} do or die.
I've got no choice but to {f:try|try}.
For {f:me|me}, the line between dream and reality was already fading.{p}

"Then what about the real Commander?"
"Ah, this thing probably killed the real one. ……………I have a proposal. How would you like to take office as the new Commander?"
Kazama said to {f:me|me}.{p}

"Hold on, please. That's way too sudden, {f:come on|really}. {f:I'm|I'm} not cut out to be Commander, {f:no way|honestly}."
"No, if you hadn't killed that Nyarinian, who knows what would've become of us... I'll report this whole affair to the Sunbararian minister. You're as good as named the next Commander. Now that that's settled, let's head back to planet Sunbararia right away. We have to prepare for the new Commander's inauguration ceremony. Now, to our homeland Sunbararia, let us return!☆"
Then Kazama... no, the Sunbararian, took out something like a patch and raised one hand.{p}

Putting on a serious face, {f:I|I} said to him,
"Kazama, those of {f:us|us} who survived have to live on, at least. I don't know what to {f:say|say} to the people of Sunbararia... {f:We|We} have to live for their sake too."
{f:I|I} put my hand on Kazama's shoulder and walked over to the window.{p}

...{f:Was|Was} {f:I|I} still alive?
I'm sure my mind wouldn't be this clear if I {f:were|were} dead.
I slowly opened my eyes.{p}

Apparently Kazama was now overcome with even greater emotion.
His green tentacles were twitching and quivering.
"Um..."
"Magnificent☆ Ah, what good fortune! That was unmistakably the Kyukyu language! Only those of royal blood can read this ancient text."
Oh boy, yet another outrageous story had come up{f:...|...}
Kazama took out a thing that looked like a patch and spoke into it.{p}

Wrapped in white light, {f:I|I} departed for Sunbararia...
{f:Yeah|Right}, rather than living out an ordinary life here on Earth, maybe a life of VIP treatment on Sunbararia wouldn't be so bad{f:.|.}
{f:Farewell, O blue Earth|Farewell, blue Earth}.{p}

{f:I|I} decided there was nothing for it but to dance.
But... what was I supposed to dance{f:?|?}
The only dance {f:I|I} knew and could actually perform was...
...The Cossack dance is the only one I know{f:!|!}
W-well, it can't be helped.{p}

Kazama watched it in silence...
What should I do?
Is it really okay for me to just keep on dancing like this{f:?|?}
Kazama went on saying nothing.
I had no idea what he was thinking, but...
At least as long as I kept this up, it seemed he wouldn't hurt me{f:.|.}
Still, my legs were getting tired{f:.|.}
...............Hm?
Kazama suddenly staggered.
His legs were wobbling.
Had watching {f:my|my} dance made him dizzy{f:?|?}
Yes!
If this went well, I might be able to escape...
But Kazama seized {f:me|me} firmly by the shoulders.{p}

Ah, this really isn't a dream after all{f:.|.}
They were marching down the hallway, tramp, tramp, tramp.
Are they heading this way{f:?|?}
Of course{f:,|,} they know the Commander came here.
...So that's why{f:.|.}
This is bad{f:...|...}{p}

In an instant, an idea popped into {f:my|my} head.
{f:I|I} hesitated over whether to go through with it, but there was no other choice.
It wasn't exactly a good idea, but it would do just fine as a stopgap in an emergency.{p}

"☆★··☆★☆·"
"☆··, ☆★·☆·?"
{f:They seemed|They seemed} to be chattering among themselves in some incomprehensible language.{p}

No way, did it figure out I'm here{f:?|?}
How did it find out{f:?|?}
What do I do!{p}

"Here goes!"
{f:I|I} summoned all my nerve and leaped out.
And I grabbed hold of the Sunbararian, who was bigger than {f:me|me}.{p}

{f:I|I} yanked on the Sunbararian's tentacles with all my might.
"☆·☆·★☆☆★·!"
It let out a strange shriek and collapsed flat on the floor.{p}

{f:I|I} took another shot at speaking Sunbararian.
"·☆·☆★·★☆·☆☆☆"
(Now, everyone. We have lost one precious Sunbararian brother, but do not grieve. He took an Earthling down with him and fell nobly in the line of duty. Let us honor him. We have a great deal of work ahead of us. Let us return to the secret base.){p}

With a high-pitched whirr, {f:I|I} was engulfed in a dazzling flash along with the Sunbararians.
Am {f:I|I} really going to end up as the Sunbararians' Commander like this{f:?|?}
What has {f:my|my} life come to...{p}

Without thinking, {f:I|I} started dancing.
And not just any dance, but a corny old folk dance...
"Tra-la-la, tra-la-la-la-la-laaa, ta-dum-ta-ta-ta☆"
Humming the melody, {f:I|I} began dancing all by myself.
I no longer felt even a shred of embarrassment.
...I wonder how long I danced.
Incredibly, the Sunbararians started dancing along with {f:me|me}{f:!|!}
Lucky! That fooled them nicely{f:.|.}
The Sunbararians are pretty good dancers{f:, too|, aren't they}.{p}

......................................Wait a {f:second|second}.
Come to think of it, I fooled them all right, but what am I supposed to do from here{f:?|?}★
Luckily the Sunbararians are lost in their dancing{f:, but|, but} the problem is what comes after{f:.|.}
So, am {f:I|I} going to stay here dancing with them forever★
Tomorrow and the day after are Saturday and Sunday, so that's fine, but what am I supposed to do on Monday{f:?|?}{p}

If anyone finds {f:me|me} dancing with weird aliens, my life is over{f:.|.}
Before that, I'll drop dead from exhaustion{f:!|!}
This isn't fair{f:!|!}
...I've got it{f:!|!}☆
All {f:I|I} have to do is lead them away while I dance like this{f:!|!}
{f:What a genius|What a genius} you are, {b} {a}☆
...Wait, come to think of it, where am I supposed to take them-m-m{f:?!|?!}
{f:I|I} really am a complete idio-o-ot{f:!|!}☆{p}

Oh no!
I had completely forgotten to take off this mask{f:.|.}
...Huh?
It won't come off!
I-it won't come off!{p}

...Come to think of it, this is strange{f:.|.}
This head felt so fishy-smelling and creepy at first, but now it fits me oddly well.
As if it were {f:my|my} own head...
And when I really think about it, it's strange{f:.|.}
How did {f:my|my} head fit inside something only the size of Kazama's head{f:?|?}
The sizes don't match{f:!|!}{p}

Mom still seemed frightened{f:.|.}
{f:I|I} pleaded with her.
"Mom! It's {f:me|me}☆ It's {b}{f:!|!}"
And then Mom came running toward {f:me|me}.{p}

Wait, what is Mom talking about{f:...|...}
Then Mom put a hand to her chin and briskly peeled off her skin.
It was that ammonite head.
"Mom joined the grown-ups at the same age you are now. I'm so happy. I wonder if there's still time to make some red-bean rice. I'll call Dad at the office and have him come home early."
Said a face identical to {f:my|my} mask.{p}

So that means {f:my|my} family was a Sunbararian family{f:?|?}
Kazama's mask won't come off because {f:I|I} was a Sunbararian?
Because {f:I|I} put on Kazama's mask right as my body was going through its adult transformation?
A feeling of utter deflation washed over {f:me|me}...
But then again, maybe this is a kind of happiness in its own way...{p}

"★"
Th-the mask won't come off!
It must be because I forced it onto my face{f:.|.}
If I go to the hospital, maybe they can do something about it.{p}

{f:I have to|I've got to} get the doctor to peel this mask off somehow.
{f:I|I} hid under the doctor's desk.
About thirty minutes must have passed{f:.|.}
Dr. Tanaka came into the room.
Dr. Tanaka is a little chubby.
The doctor's hobbies are a bit nerdy too, but {f:I|I} like Dr. Tanaka{f:.|.}
The doctor switched on the light.{p}

{f:I|I} slowly opened my eyes.
...Have {f:I|I} been asleep this whole time{f:?|?}
Dr. Tanaka was peering down at me.
"Doctor☆ {f:I|I} got my old face back, didn't I★"
Dr. Tanaka laughed and said,{p}

"M-my body won't move!"
{f:My|My} body was strapped to the bed with belts.
"It would be a problem if you got away. So I had you tied down. You're precious research material, after all. Now behave yourself."{p}

Dr. Tanaka's loud laughter echoed through the room.
It seemed {f:I|I} would go on living as the doctor's research material.
Looking like this, no one will ever believe me again, no matter what I say{f:.|.}
This isn't fair☆{p}

Is it always this quiet inside a TV station{f:?|?}
I guess it's different from a movie studio.
Thinking such things, {f:I|I} hurried on.
"This is {f:it|it}..."
With my hand on the door, {f:I|I} thought,
Oh no, I have to take off the mask...{p}
